<%- include('partials/header') %>
<main id="main-content">
  <section class="page-intro">
    <div class="container">
      <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><ol><li><a href="/">Home</a></li><li aria-current="page">Operators</li></ol></nav>
      <p class="eyebrow">For vessel operators, ship managers, crewing teams &amp; agents</p>
      <h1>Prepare crew connectivity before departure.</h1>
      <p class="lead">Give joining crew a clear path to mobile data and setup instructions before they travel. Discuss connectivity for one crew change or a pattern of repeat rotations.</p>
      <div class="inline-links"><a class="button button-primary" href="<%= site.inquiryUrls.connectivity %>" data-event="operator_inquiry">Discuss Crew Connectivity</a><a class="text-link" href="<%= site.shopUrl %>" data-event="buy_esim_click">See eSIM Coverage</a></div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="operator-use-cases-heading">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">Where connectivity helps</p><h2 id="operator-use-cases-heading">From the joining instructions to the port gate.</h2></div><p>For manning companies and crewing departments, connectivity belongs in the same preparation as flights, meeting points and local contacts.</p></div>
      <div class="grid-three">
        <article class="feature-card"><p class="eyebrow">Before embarkation</p><h3>Send the setup path early.</h3><p>Share the Amicus store and device-check guidance with joining crew. Checking the phone and plan while a reliable internet connection is available can reduce reliance on finding a SIM kiosk after landing.</p></article>
        <article class="feature-card"><p class="eyebrow">During travel</p><h3>Plan for every travel country.</h3><p>Home, a connecting airport and the joining port may need different coverage. A regional or wider plan may suit the itinerary where all destinations are included. Check each leg before ordering.</p></article>
        <article class="feature-card"><p class="eyebrow">During port calls</p><h3>Keep shore time connected.</h3><p>Mobile data can help crew reach their coordinator, use maps and contact family ashore. It depends on the plan and local signal; it does not replace onboard satellite connectivity.</p></article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section section-soft" aria-labelledby="crew-ordering-heading">
    <div class="container split">
      <div><p class="eyebrow">The current crew purchasing path</p><h2 id="crew-ordering-heading">A coordinated offer. Individual setup.</h2><p>The Amicus eSIM store supports discussing batches of individual crew discount codes. Code values, limits and expiry are agreed for the requirement.</p><%- include('partials/media', { media: media.operations }) %></div>
      <div class="stack">
        <ol class="numbered-list">
          <li><h3>Outline the rotation.</h3><p>Send the travel countries, departure dates, approximate crew count and how often the journey repeats.</p></li>
          <li><h3>Agree the code arrangement.</h3><p>Discuss an individual-code batch and distribute the agreed codes with the store's compatibility and setup guidance.</p></li>
          <li><h3>Crew complete their own purchase.</h3><p>Each crew member uses their own email, checks the phone and plan, and places the order. Activation details follow successful payment and provisioning.</p></li>
        </ol>
        <p>Need centralized payment, invoicing or a different distribution process? Include that in your inquiry so we can confirm what can be arranged. The store does not currently provide a fleet usage or activation dashboard.</p>
        <div class="inline-links"><a class="button button-primary" href="<%= site.inquiryUrls.connectivity %>" data-event="operator_inquiry">Discuss Crew Connectivity</a><a class="text-link" href="<%= site.businessUrl %>" data-event="operator_inquiry">See the store's crew ordering details</a></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="operator-coordination-heading">
    <div class="container split">
      <div><p class="eyebrow">Beyond mobile data</p><h2 id="operator-coordination-heading">Keep crew-change information together.</h2></div>
      <div class="stack"><p>When vessel details, travel stages and updates are scattered across messages, each handover needs another check. Amicus Crew Change provides a shared workflow for participating crew and their coordinators.</p><p>Explore how it works before opening an account. Operator, agent and other coordination roles require the appropriate invitation; local transport and port arrangements must still be confirmed.</p><a class="text-link" href="<%= site.crewLandingUrl %>">Explore Amicus Crew Change</a></div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section section-dark"><div class="container split"><div><p class="eyebrow">For the next rotation</p><h2>Start with the itinerary and crew count.</h2><p>Tell us who is travelling, where they need data and whether you expect the same route again.</p></div><div><a class="button button-light" href="<%= site.inquiryUrls.connectivity %>" data-event="operator_inquiry">Discuss Crew Connectivity</a></div></div></section>
</main>
<%- include('partials/footer') %>